<!--
  Every user-facing string in the mobile app. Flat, no library — the same shape the web
  uses in webApp/src/i18n/en.ts, and deliberately the same key names with dots swapped for
  underscores (Res.string accessors cannot carry a dot). Keeping them mechanically
  parallel is what lets the Arabic in ar.ts be reused rather than re-translated, and lets
  the two products be diffed for drift.

  Voice rules, from design doc 1 and unchanged here: say "Trip", never "Album"; second
  person, present tense; errors name the thing and the fix; no exclamation marks except
  the two celebration moments.

  Animation labels (navIndicator, skeletonSweep, dockChevron and friends) are NOT strings
  in this sense — they are debug identifiers Compose never shows anyone. They stay inline.
-->
